--------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Save-path catalogue (crates/hoard-manifest/data/)

   Files: ludusavi-catalog.json.zst, ludusavi-titles.json.zst

   Derived from the Ludusavi manifest (https://github.com/mtkennerly/ludusavi-manifest) 
   by mtkennerly. The manifest tooling is MIT-licensed;
   the underlying save-path data is sourced from PCGamingWiki
   (https://www.pcgamingwiki.com/) and is licensed
   CC BY-NC-SA 3.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/3.0/).

   Attribution: PCGamingWiki contributors, via the Ludusavi manifest.

   IMPORTANT: the NonCommercial clause. CC BY-NC-SA 3.0 forbids use
   "primarily intended for or directed toward commercial advantage or private
   monetary compensation". Shipping this data inside a build that is
   distributed alongside a paid subscription is not clearly permitted by that
   licence.

   Build the crate with `--no-default-features` (feature `bundled-catalog`
   off) to produce a binary that carries no catalogue and downloads it at
   first run instead. See crates/hoard-manifest/data/README.md.

2. Rust and JavaScript dependencies

   Their licences (MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD, ISC and others) are those declared
   in Cargo.toml and package.json, which pin the exact version of every
   dependency. Neither a vendored crates tree nor node_modules is
   distributed with this software or checked into the repository, so the
   licence texts themselves do not travel with a build; run `cargo vendor`
   or `pnpm install` against those manifests to obtain them. Shipping a
   THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES file with each package is still owed.

3. Game cover art

   Fetched at runtime from third-party providers and cached locally on the
